-- ============================================================================
-- RC7 PROFESSIONAL DEEP SEED: Well Test Analysis, intermediate tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions. Structure generated from the tier's
-- manifest.json.
--
-- What this tier owns: the derivative as the DIAGNOSIS. The Bourdet
-- three-point rule and its smoothing window; the slope alphabet and the order
-- flow regimes must occur in; the engine's own classifier read honestly, band
-- by band and rule by rule; the boundary gallery, in which a
-- sealing fault's late semilog line reports a bit over half the permeability
-- and inverts the skin again; a fracture, whose semilog reading claims
-- 26.266915078269914 mD on 5 mD rock; the horizontal well's three regimes; and
-- the closed rectangle, the one place in this course where a well test
-- measures a volume and gets it right to a few thousandths of a percent.
--
-- THE CLASSIFIER DEFECT THIS COURSE FOUND, AND THE FIX IT SHIPPED WITH. A
-- slope band is necessary and not sufficient: a transition between two regimes
-- has a well defined local slope that usually falls inside one. A steep FALL
-- between two regimes landed in the constant-pressure band, and a slow RISE
-- between two plateaus landed in the bilinear band, so the engine reported a
-- recharge boundary on infinite-acting tests and bilinear flow on wells with
-- no fracture: six of the seven fixtures in this course carried at least one
-- regime that is not there, and so did the Suite's Well Test Analysis Studio.
-- Two ordering rules now catch both, relabelling to a transition rather than
-- discarding the segment, and they remove eight labels while leaving every
-- genuine regime alone (petrolord-suite PR #336, mirrored here).
--
-- ONE FALSE LABEL SURVIVES AND IS TAUGHT. The fault fixture's first segment is
-- still called linear flow where it is the roll-off of a storage unit slope.
-- A fracture's linear flow legitimately comes first too, so nothing about the
-- ORDER separates them; the PRESSURE curve does, because during storage the
-- pressure and its derivative coincide, and the classifier is handed only the
-- derivative. A regime label needs five things before it is a diagnosis, and
-- the software supplies three of them.
--
-- Answer keys live only here and in academy_quiz_questions, which has no
-- client SELECT policy.
-- ============================================================================

